WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
Extension can produce normal faults, down-dropped grabens, and raised

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:08.860
horsts. Shortening produces folds and thrusts. Sideways shear produces

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:13.240
strike-slip displacement. Watch marker layers to define relative movement.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.520
Erosion exposes resistant inclined layers and weaker fractured zones.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:20.800
A dip slope follows bedding. A ridge is not

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.580
automatically an anticline: resistance and erosion shape landscapes. Bedding

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.320
and later cleavage can differ. A fault is younger

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.120
than the layers it cuts. A continuous unit sealing

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.300
the break is younger than the observed slip. New

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.900
England records collision and metamorphism, then later rifting. Combine

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:41.900
maps, fabrics, and cross-cutting relations; one rock name cannot

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.360
establish every event.
